IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1 -- piece dg11, Subchapter XVIII:
-- section 395, "Corporations using 'trust' in name, advertisements and otherwise".
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- The source is the plain-text rendering de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt (not the official text). `-- src:N | ...` is line N of it.
--
-- OUT OF RANGE (taken as plain inputs, never recomputed):
--   * "regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956, 12 U.S.C. § 1841 et seq., or § 10 of the Home Owners' Loan Act,
--     12 U.S.C. § 1467a et seq." -- federal statutes, not among the inputs: a BOOLEAN fact.
--   * "the Savings and Loan Holding Company Act" (subsection (b), last sentence) -- a federal statute, not among the inputs.
--     The text names it differently from subsections (a), (b) first sentence, (c) and (d) (which name § 10 of the Home Owners' Loan Act),
--     so it is its own input (Fork register F-395-1).
--   * the form of the report "which shall be prescribed by the Commissioner" -- an instrument of the State Bank Commissioner, not among
--     the inputs: whether a report is in that form is a BOOLEAN fact.
--   * the determination "by the Director of the Division of Corporations and the State Bank Commissioner" (subsection (d)(3)) -- a judgment
--     the text hands to two officials, taken as a conditional input (that they have so determined), never guessed.
-- The heading speaks of "violations and penalties", but the text of section 395 states no penalty (NOTES.md, finding on s 395).

§ `Section 395(d) - where the requirements and restrictions of (a) and (b) do not apply`

-- src:2095 | (d) The requirements and restrictions set forth above in subsections (a) and (b) of this section shall not apply to, and shall not be construed to prevent the use of the word “trust” as part of the name of, a corporation that is not subject to the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner of this State and that is not regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956, 12 U.S.C. § 1841 et seq., or § 10 of the Home Owners’ Loan Act, 12 U.S.C. § 1467a et seq., where use of the word “trust” as part of such corporation’s name clearly:
-- src:2096 | (1) Does not refer to a trust business;
-- src:2097 | (2) Is not likely to mislead the public into believing that the nature of the business of the corporation includes activities that fall under the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner of this State or that are regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956, 12 U.S.C. § 1841 et seq., or § 10 of the Home Owners’ Loan Act, 12 U.S.C. § 1467a et seq.; and
-- src:2098 | (3) Will not otherwise lead to a pattern and practice of abuse that might cause harm to the interests of the public or the State, as determined by the Director of the Division of Corporations and the State Bank Commissioner.
-- Gloss: the exception is cumulative: the corporation is neither supervised nor regulated, AND its use of "trust" clearly meets all of (1), (2) and (3).
-- The word "clearly" governs the three limbs together; it is read as a condition on each (Fork register F-395-2).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 395(d) (src:2095-2098)
GIVEN `the corporation is subject to the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956 or § 10 of the Home Owners' Loan Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its use of the word trust clearly does not refer to a trust business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its use of the word trust is clearly not likely to mislead the public about the supervised or regulated nature of its business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Director of the Division of Corporations and the State Bank Commissioner have determined that its use of the word trust will not lead to a pattern and practice of abuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 395(d) the requirements and restrictions of subsections (a) and (b) do not apply to the corporation`
    `the corporation is subject to the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner`
    `the corporation is regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956 or § 10 of the Home Owners' Loan Act`
    `its use of the word trust clearly does not refer to a trust business`
    `its use of the word trust is clearly not likely to mislead the public about the supervised or regulated nature of its business`
    `the Director of the Division of Corporations and the State Bank Commissioner have determined that its use of the word trust will not lead to a pattern and practice of abuse` MEANS
        (NOT `the corporation is subject to the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner`)
    AND (NOT `the corporation is regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956 or § 10 of the Home Owners' Loan Act`)
    AND `its use of the word trust clearly does not refer to a trust business`
    AND `its use of the word trust is clearly not likely to mislead the public about the supervised or regulated nature of its business`
    AND `the Director of the Division of Corporations and the State Bank Commissioner have determined that its use of the word trust will not lead to a pattern and practice of abuse`

§ `Section 395(a) - supervision by the State Bank Commissioner; reports`

-- src:2092 | (a) Except as provided below in subsection (d) of this section, every corporation of this State using the word “trust” as part of its name, except a corporation regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956, 12 U.S.C. § 1841 et seq., or § 10 of the Home Owners’ Loan Act, 12 U.S.C. § 1467a et seq., as those statutes shall from time to time be amended, shall be under the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner of this State and shall make not less than 2 reports during each year to the Commissioner, according to the form which shall be prescribed by the Commissioner, verified by the oaths or affirmations of the president or vice-president, and the treasurer or secretary of the corporation, and attested by the signatures of at least 3 directors.
-- The corporation's side: it is under supervision and must report; the Commissioner's side: the Commissioner supervises and receives the reports.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 395(a) (src:2092)
GIVEN `the corporation uses the word trust as part of its name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956 or § 10 of the Home Owners' Loan Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements and restrictions of subsections (a) and (b) do not apply to the corporation under subsection (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 395(a) the corporation is under the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner and must make reports to the Commissioner`
    `the corporation uses the word trust as part of its name`
    `the corporation is regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956 or § 10 of the Home Owners' Loan Act`
    `the requirements and restrictions of subsections (a) and (b) do not apply to the corporation under subsection (d)` MEANS
        `the corporation uses the word trust as part of its name`
    AND (NOT `the corporation is regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956 or § 10 of the Home Owners' Loan Act`)
    AND (NOT `the requirements and restrictions of subsections (a) and (b) do not apply to the corporation under subsection (d)`)

-- "during each year": the text does not say which year (the calendar year, or a year counted from some other date). The rule counts the reports made in the year the caller names (Fork register F-395-3).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 395(a) (src:2092)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 395(a) the fewest reports that the corporation must make to the Commissioner during each year` MEANS 2

@ref 8 Del. C. § 395(a) (src:2092)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 395(a) the fewest directors whose signatures must attest each report` MEANS 3

-- src:2092 | according to the form which shall be prescribed by the Commissioner, verified by the oaths or affirmations of the president or vice-president, and the treasurer or secretary of the corporation, and attested by the signatures of at least 3 directors.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 395(a) (src:2092)
DECLARE `s 395(a) Report made to the State Bank Commissioner` HAS
    `report is in the form prescribed by the Commissioner`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `report is verified by the oath or affirmation of the president or vice-president` IS A BOOLEAN
    `report is verified by the oath or affirmation of the treasurer or secretary`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `directors whose signatures attest the report`                                  IS A NUMBER

-- Gloss: two verifications are needed: one by "the president or vice-president" AND one by "the treasurer or secretary". Attestation by
-- "at least 3 directors" is a count that reaches 3 (three is enough).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 395(a) (src:2092)
GIVEN report IS A `s 395(a) Report made to the State Bank Commissioner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 395(a) the report is in the form, verified and attested as required` report MEANS
        report's `report is in the form prescribed by the Commissioner`
    AND report's `report is verified by the oath or affirmation of the president or vice-president`
    AND report's `report is verified by the oath or affirmation of the treasurer or secretary`
    AND (report's `directors whose signatures attest the report` AT LEAST `s 395(a) the fewest directors whose signatures must attest each report`)

-- "not less than 2 reports during each year": reaching 2 compliant reports in the year is enough.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 395(a) (src:2092)
GIVEN `the number of reports made during the year that are in the form, verified and attested as required` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 395(a) the corporation has made enough reports during the year` `the number of reports made during the year that are in the form, verified and attested as required` MEANS
    `the number of reports made during the year that are in the form, verified and attested as required` AT LEAST `s 395(a) the fewest reports that the corporation must make to the Commissioner during each year`

§ `Section 395(b) - use of the word trust in a corporate name`

-- src:2093 | (b) Except as provided below in subsection (d) of this section, no corporation of this State shall use the word “trust” as part of its name, except a corporation reporting to and under the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner of this State or a corporation regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956, 12 U.S.C. § 1841 et seq., or § 10 of the Home Owners’ Loan Act, 12 U.S.C. § 1467a et seq., as those statutes shall from time to time be amended.
-- Gloss: the corporation may use "trust" in its name if it reports to and is under the supervision of the Commissioner, or is regulated under the
-- federal statutes, or is within the subsection (d) exception. The Commissioner's and the State's side: no-right in the corporation otherwise.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 395(b) (src:2093)
GIVEN `the corporation reports to and is under the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956 or § 10 of the Home Owners' Loan Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements and restrictions of subsections (a) and (b) do not apply to the corporation under subsection (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 395(b) the corporation may use the word trust as part of its name`
    `the corporation reports to and is under the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner`
    `the corporation is regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956 or § 10 of the Home Owners' Loan Act`
    `the requirements and restrictions of subsections (a) and (b) do not apply to the corporation under subsection (d)` MEANS
        `the corporation reports to and is under the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner`
    OR  `the corporation is regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956 or § 10 of the Home Owners' Loan Act`
    OR  `the requirements and restrictions of subsections (a) and (b) do not apply to the corporation under subsection (d)`

-- src:2093 | Except as provided below in subsection (d) of this section, the name of any such corporation shall not be amended so as to include the word “trust” unless such corporation shall report to and be under the supervision of the Commissioner, or unless it is regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956 or the Savings and Loan Holding Company Act.
-- Gloss: this sentence names "the Savings and Loan Holding Company Act", where the rest of the section names § 10 of the Home Owners' Loan Act; they are two inputs.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 395(b) (src:2093)
GIVEN `the corporation reports to and is under the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956 or the Savings and Loan Holding Company Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements and restrictions of subsections (a) and (b) do not apply to the corporation under subsection (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 395(b) the corporation's name may be amended so as to include the word trust`
    `the corporation reports to and is under the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner`
    `the corporation is regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956 or the Savings and Loan Holding Company Act`
    `the requirements and restrictions of subsections (a) and (b) do not apply to the corporation under subsection (d)` MEANS
        `the corporation reports to and is under the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner`
    OR  `the corporation is regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956 or the Savings and Loan Holding Company Act`
    OR  `the requirements and restrictions of subsections (a) and (b) do not apply to the corporation under subsection (d)`

§ `Section 395(c) - acting as a trust company`

-- src:2094 | (c) No corporation of this State, except corporations reporting to and under the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner of this State or corporations regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956, 12 U.S.C. § 1841 et seq., or § 10 of the Home Owners’ Loan Act, 12 U.S.C. § 1467a et seq., as those statutes shall from time to time be amended, shall advertise or put forth any sign as a trust company, or in any way solicit or receive deposits or transact business as a trust company.
-- The subsection (d) exception is stated for subsections (a) and (b) only ("above in subsections (a) and (b)"), so it is not an input here.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 395(c) (src:2094)
GIVEN `the corporation reports to and is under the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956 or § 10 of the Home Owners' Loan Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 395(c) the corporation may advertise, solicit or receive deposits or transact business as a trust company`
    `the corporation reports to and is under the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner`
    `the corporation is regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956 or § 10 of the Home Owners' Loan Act` MEANS
        `the corporation reports to and is under the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner`
    OR  `the corporation is regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956 or § 10 of the Home Owners' Loan Act`
